      "statement": "SaiLoR is a tool for conducting Systematic Literature Reviews (SLR); a project is a project.json file holding the annotation schema (a nested, cardinality-controlled taxonomy) and paper metadata, with a sibling annotations/ folder holding the actual annotation data, one file per paper per reviewer plus a consolidated file, so two reviewers working on different papers rarely collide in git.",
